# e09_event.gbnf: the four literals of rules_e09.c, letter for letter, in the house
# shape: one JSON object with one "decision" key. The order is the rule's name table,
# NONE first, so the CI stub answers {"decision":"NONE"} on every row it is asked. ws
# admits spaces and tabs only, never a newline, so the longest answer, FREEFALL, stays
# inside the n_predict of 8 tokens; the chapter's pitfall on tokenizers says how to count.
root     ::= "{" ws "\"decision\"" ws ":" ws decision ws "}"
decision ::= "\"NONE\"" | "\"TAP\"" | "\"TILT\"" | "\"FREEFALL\""
ws       ::= [ \t]*
